 "argument": "Phi(z) = s - sum_r omega_r g_r with A_ext^T omega = e_s to eps_w.  For any feasible z in box(h): s(z) = Phi(z) + sum_r omega_r g_r >= Phi(z) + alpha_min G(z) with G the sum of the variant rows and the two aux rows (dominance terms dropped, omega >= 0 there), and Phi(z) >= s-hat - eps_0 - eps_w h - Hbar h^2.  Either G >= T(h) and s >= s-hat, or every A22 Krawczyk row is in [0, T+g_max] so ||z - z-hat||_inf <= kappa(T+g_max)/(1-beta) = psi < h; iterating the dichotomy drives the radius to x* <= r_N and A22 finishes.  NO break set, stratum or selection of maintained rows enters the argument, so one certificate covers the whole lattice."
